the other big story tonight of today  rather of course is a republican  national convention president trump will  officially  accept his nomination for a second term  this evening against the backdrop of  this historic storm  an unprecedented pandemic and national  calls for racial justice in this country  vice president mike pence addressed all  three of those issues in his speech to  the convention last night  he praised the president's work over the  past four years and strongly criticized  democratic nominee joe biden paula reed  has  more on this story from the white house  in this country we mourn with those who  mourn we grieve with those who grieve  headlining the third night of the  convention vice president mike pence  framed the administration's handling of  the pandemic as  ahead of the curve before the first case  of the coronavirus spread within the  united states  the president took unprecedented action  and suspended  all travel from china i have the mask  right here but it was months before the  president acknowledged the severity of  the virus  and endorsed preventative measures like  wearing a mask  pence was the only speaker to mention  kenosha wisconsin  yet another city gripped by protests  over the shooting of a black man  jacob blake by police so let me be clear  the violence must stop whether in  minneapolis  portland or kenosha too many heroes have  died defending our freedom  to see americans strike each other down  we will have  law and order on the streets of this  country  but he made no mention of the shooting  that prompted the protest  or any of the black men and women who  have died at the hands of law  enforcement  and he said that a biden administration  would double down on policies that are  leading to the violence in american  cities  ignoring that it is under president  trump that the violence is occurring  the hard truth is  you won't be safe in joe biden's america  the night also saw a concerted effort to  reach out to female voters  who currently prefer joe biden according  to recent polls  i have a nine-month-old daughter she's a  beautiful  sweet little girl and i choose  to work for this president for her  a woman in a leadership role can still  seem novel  not so for president trump for decades  he has elevated women to senior  positions  in business and in government  later tonight president trump will take  the stage here on the south lawn of the  white house  to give his acceptance speech and make  that critical pitch for a second term  he's expected to speak in front of a  crowd of over a thousand people  the white house says all of them will be  tested for covid  gail paul the cdc is under fire for the  changes that they've made in testing  what are you hearing about these changes  and how did it come about  well gail in a stunning reversal the cdc  now says even if you've been exposed to  someone with the virus  that you don't need to get tested if  you're not showing symptoms  the cdc quietly posted this revision to  their guidance on their website but i've  been speaking with dr anthony fauci this  morning and he tells me that he was not  at an august 20th meeting where these  revisions were discussed  by the task force he was undergoing  surgery for a polyp on his vocal cord  now he tells me he's concerned that  these revisions could be interpreted as  lessening the importance of asymptomatic  spread  now president trump's re-election  chances have of course been harmed  by the pandemic he has repeatedly called  for less  testing the democrats have blasted this  revision saying that the president now  has the cdc  carrying out his political agenda though  a senior white house official insists  that these changes were made through all  the standard protocols  but paul from all that we've been told  about this uh  covet 19 do you think it sends mixed  messages  on an already very confusing situation  to test to not to test who gets tested  what test is effective absolutely gail  and from the start of this pandemic that  is what we have seen from this white  house the one consistent thing has been  mixed messages do as we say not as we do  quietly changing these key guidelines  when you clearly really don't have  consensus among your top officials it's  what we've seen since the beginning  but you can't ignore the science of this  of this covid19  wear your mask at the white house last  night most people in that crowd  were not wearing masks and they were not  social distancing at  vice president pence's address last  night  that's absolutely right no it is it's  very surprising again often and we've  asked the vice president this  uh publicly why is it so often they give  us guidance and then they don't follow  it everything from shaking hands  to wearing masks to social distancing  and the administration has really not  had any answers  all right i say again pay attention to  the science thank you paula reed  thank you very much we'll talk with you  a little bit later on
 

